    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50655" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππ-αγρέται</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>,
			οἱ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρέω</span>)
		three officers at Lacedaemon, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>who chose</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				300
			</span></i>, the flower of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφηβοι</span>,
				<i>to serve as a body-guard for the kings</i> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.1
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.3.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lac.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archyt.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.1.138
			</span></i>: sg., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.38
			</span></i> (unless it be pr. n.).</div>
